[gd_scene format=3 uid="uid://bq3hrvn7y8kda"]

; THE MODAL MOVESET'S SHOWCASE YARD. Replaces test_level.tscn as what
; `scenes/main.tscn` loads.
;
; ─── WHY THIS IS A REBUILD AND NOT A PORT ───────────────────────────────────
;
; `test_level.tscn` is four corridors (A/B/C/D) hanging off a hub, and each one
; was built around a verb that no longer exists: `BRunWall` is the wall run,
; `AGlideCoin*` is the glide, and North/South were grapple anchors. Three
; deleted abilities out of four zones, so there was nothing to repoint.
;
; It is kept on disk, unreferenced except by `scenes/legacy_main.tscn`, which is
; the old suite's fixture. It is the record of the Mario moveset.
;
; ─── THE SHAPE, WHICH THE DESIGN DOC DICTATES ───────────────────────────────
;
; One OPEN yard, not corridors — the doc's "world itself is the puzzle" with
; "density of weight-reactive terrain" named as the level-design KPI. Every
; setup below is stated as a PROBLEM rather than a lock: any application of the
; weight rules that reaches the goal counts.
;
; Each threshold is a MEASURED number, not an invented one. All of these came
; off `tests/greybox_probe.gd`:
;
;   walking                      15.0 m/s      a walking jump covers  15.5 m
;   charge on the flat           20.0 m/s      a charge-jump covers   21.2 m
;   charge down a 15 degree ramp 26.0 m/s      the hero's mass is     10
;   a hop-stomp is worth            7 momentum, reaching  1.25 m
;   a stomp after a 12 m drop      140 momentum, reaching 10.00 m
;
; ─── THE EIGHT PROBLEMS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
;   1  charge down the ramp into RampWall      break_speed 22: flat charge
;                                              does 20, off the ramp 26
;   2  the 18 m gap to SouthIsland             a walking jump does 15.5,
;                                              a charge-jump 21.2
;   3  ram PlateCrate on to Plate, ride the    required_mass 14 against a hero
;      lift, slam SealedLid from the tower     of 10; strike_momentum 120
;   4  the see-saw and the 8-mass crate        carry_max_mass 10
;   5  CrumbleSpan over the trench             break_mass 20: holds the hero
;                                              at 10, not the giant at 40
;   6  lure the giant through MassWall         break_mass 30, and he walks at
;                                              3 m/s so no speed gate can work
;   7  the rail off the ramp deck              the slope decides the speed
;   8  pay the exit                            250 against 310 on the floor
;
; ─── TWO LAWS THAT SHAPED THE GEOMETRY ──────────────────────────────────────
;
; **There is no death, and ejection from an arena is banned.** So every hole in
; this yard has a floor and a staircase out of it — the trench and the gap both.
; Falling in costs you the climb, which is a live in-arena penalty, and never
; travel time. The perimeter is walled for the same reason: there is nothing to
; fall off, because falling off the world with no death is an infinite fall.
;
; **A gate must guard something optional, never the critical path.** The exit is
; on the main ground. The charge-jump gates the ISLAND TREASURE, which is worth
; 70 and is skippable — so a player who cannot clear 18 m is poorer, not stuck.

