; ───────────────────────────── problem 3: ram, ride, slam — a three-step problem
;
; The only setup here that chains three verbs, and the one that proves the weight
; layer is a vocabulary rather than a pile of props:
;
;   PlateCrate weighs 16, which is OVER carry_max_mass (10), so it cannot be
;   picked up — it has to be RAMMED (weight rule 2). The plate wants 14, which
;   is over the hero's own 10, so standing on it is not enough either (rule 1).
;   It latches, the lift rises to the tower top, and from 14 m up a slam is
;   worth 140 against SealedLid's 120.

[node name="Tower" type="CSGBox3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 24, 7, -10)
use_collision = true
size = Vector3(8, 14, 8)
material = SubResource("MatTower")

; Bridges the lift to the tower's east face, because a lift that arrives two
; metres short of the thing it serves is a lip the player falls off.
[node name="TowerLanding" type="CSGBox3D" parent="."]
